Subject: dialog-v2: aria-label, viewport size, viewport-bounded cards, host-owned failure card

What: `DialogV2` takes `aria-label` for a dialog that mounts no Title, and
`size: "viewport"` (min(100vw - 64px, 1400px) by 100vh - 64px). The normal and
large cards are bounded by the viewport (min(100vw - 16px, 480px) by
min(100vh - 16px, 368px); min(100vw - 32px, 640px) by min(100vh - 32px, 480px))
instead of fixed 480x368 and 640x480. The `.ui-dialog-error` rules move from
components/dialog.css to context/dialog.css, which context/dialog.tsx imports.
Why: Kobalte names a dialog only from a mounted Title (axe aria-dialog-name),
and a command palette or a provider connect card has none. An image mark-up
editor needs the viewport. A fixed 480px card overflows a 390px phone layout.
The failure card is rendered by the dialog host, so its sheet loads with the
host whichever dialog generation an app renders.

